tellraw @a {"text": "Technology: The counterweight trebuchet", "color": "gold", "bold": true}
tellraw @a {"text": "Counterweight trebuchet and a breached wall.", "color": "white"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Byzantine, Islamic and Crusader Levant, traction trebuchet from China (4th century BCE) via the Avars (6th century); counterweight type by the 1180s", "color": "yellow"}
tellraw @a {"text": "A beam on an axle with a heavy hinged counterweight on the short arm and a sling on the", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "long arm. The biggest threw 100-kg stones over 200 metres and could batter a wall to", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "rubble in days.", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "The counterweight (sand or stone in a box, up to 10 tonnes) falls, whipping the long arm", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "up; the sling trails and then releases its load when the sling's loop slips off a hook set", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "at the chosen angle. Range is tuned by the sling length and the hook angle, and the hinged", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "box keeps the energy release efficient.", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "See it in context: /function ac:holy_land/acre", "color": "aqua"}
